WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.812
The ROWS frame counts ordered rows.

00:00:02.812 --> 00:00:06.122
Two preceding means up to two earlier rows.

00:00:06.122 --> 00:00:13.497
It does not mean two days, two hours, or two months unless every time unit has exactly one row.

00:00:13.497 --> 00:00:17.382
This distinction matters when the sequence has gaps.

00:00:17.382 --> 00:00:23.192
Window functions preserve detail rows while calculating across a related set.

00:00:23.192 --> 00:00:28.122
PARTITION BY defines independent groups, ORDER BY defines sequence,

00:00:28.122 --> 00:00:33.767
and the frame defines which neighboring rows participate.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:38.240
Those three choices are part of the business rule, not just syntax.
